oints \u2014 so it doesn't qualify for Chicken Hand, because Chicken Hand replaces zero-fan hands.\n\nThus, you cannot reach 8 points.\n\nAlternatively, if you **do not Peng W8**, and just **Pass**, you keep flexibility, but you're not improving.\n\nBut note: **you only have two tiles in hand: W8,W8** \u2014 you must either Peng or Pass.\n\nIf you Peng, you commit to a hand that likely cannot reach 8 points.\n\nBut perhaps you missed something.\n\nWait \u2014 look at **your own game history**: you played `Play W3`, `Play B7`, etc., and you did `Chi B3`, `Chi W5`, `Peng T4`\n\nSo all melds are exposed.\n\nAlso, **unshown tiles**: W7:1, W8:2, W9:3 \u2014 so W8 is available.\n\nBut here's a key point: **is there a possibility that you can win later with more points?**\n\nBut currently, after Peng, you\u2019ll have only 7 points max.\n\nUnless... do you have a concealed kong opportunity later? Unlikely.\n\nAnother thought: **Dragon Pung (2 points)** \u2014 you don\u2019t have any dragon meld.\n\nBut you discarded J1, J3 \u2014 so no.\n\nPerhaps **Seat Wind or Prevalent Wind**?\n\n- Prevalent Wind: West (F3)\n- Your Seat Wind: East (F1)\n\nDo you have any wind pungs? No \u2014 you discarded F1,F2,F3,F4 \u2014 so you had them but didn\u2019t pung.\n\nSo no.\n\nThus, **any completed hand will score at most 7 points**, hence **cannot win legally** under MCR rules (minimum 8 points).\n\nTherefore, **Peng W8 is pointless**, as it commits you to a non-winning hand.\n\nMoreover, if you pass, you keep the option open \u2014 but you have only W8,W8 \u2014 if you don\u2019t Peng, you must discard one W8.\n\nBut that might allow opponents to complete their hands.\n\nBut your **only choices are Peng W8 or Pass**.\n\nSince **Peng leads to a dead-end hand (cannot reach 8 points)**, and **Pass allows you to continue without committing**, **Pass is better**.\n\nBut wait \u2014 is there a chance that after Peng, you draw a tile that gives a new pattern?\n\nAfter Peng, you\u2019ll draw a 